-- title:
--   Kaimanovich–Vershik (as Erschler–Zheng recall it, pp. 9–10) — the Poisson boundary is non-trivial iff some shift-invariant event has probability strictly between 0 and 1
-- statement:
--   Let $\Gamma$ be a countable group with the discrete $\sigma$-algebra and $\mu$ a probability on $\Gamma$ (`IsProbability`). Then the Poisson boundary of $(\Gamma, \mu)$ is non-trivial (`HasNontrivialPoissonBoundary`), that is, some bounded $\mu$-harmonic function $f : \Gamma \to \mathbb R$ is not constant on the submonoid generated by the support of $\mu$, if and only if there are a measurable set $A \subseteq \Gamma^{\mathbb N}$ of trajectories (for the product $\sigma$-algebra) that is invariant under the shift, $\mathfrak s^{-1}(A) = A$ for $\mathfrak s(w_0, w_1, \ldots) = (w_1, w_2, \ldots)$ (`IsShiftInvariant`), and a point $x \in \Gamma$ with $0 < \mathbb P_x(A) < 1$. Here $\mathbb P_x$ (`pathMeasure μ x`) is the law of the trajectory $(x, xX_1, xX_1X_2, \ldots)$ of the $\mu$-random walk started at $x$, the steps $X_i$ independent with law $\mu$.
--
--   Erschler and Zheng, pp. 9–10: “There is a correspondence between $\mathcal I$ and the space of bounded $\mu$-harmonic functions on $\Gamma$. In particular, the invariant $\sigma$-field $\mathcal I$ is trivial (i.e. any event $A \in \mathcal I$ satisfies $\mathbb P_x(A) = 0$ or 1) if and only if all bounded $\mu$-harmonic functions are constant, see [36].”
--
--   The statement is the quoted equivalence with both sides negated: $\mathcal I$ is non-trivial when one of its events has $0 < \mathbb P_x(A) < 1$ for some $x$, and the boundary is non-trivial in the sense of the bundle (Walks bundle note).
-- source:
--   Kaimanovich, V. A. and Vershik, A. M., Random walks on discrete groups: boundary and entropy, Ann. Probab. 11 (1983) 457–490, https://doi.org/10.1214/aop/1176993497, pp. 9–10, , as recalled in Erschler, A. and Zheng, T., Growth of periodic Grigorchuk groups, Invent. Math. 219 (2020) 1069–1155, https://doi.org/10.1007/s00222-019-00922-0 (arXiv:1802.09077v2, whose page numbers are used), pp. 9–10

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ErschlerZheng_Walks
open ErschlerZheng

namespace KaimanovichVershik

theorem hasNontrivialPoissonBoundary_iff_exists_isShiftInvariant_pathMeasure_pos_lt_one {Γ : Type*}
    [Group Γ] [Countable Γ] [MeasurableSpace Γ] [DiscreteMeasurableSpace Γ] (μ : Γ → ℝ)
    (hμ : IsProbability μ) :
    HasNontrivialPoissonBoundary μ ↔
      ∃ A : Set (ℕ → Γ), MeasurableSet A ∧ IsShiftInvariant A ∧
        ∃ x : Γ, 0 < pathMeasure μ x A ∧ pathMeasure μ x A < 1 := by
  sorry

end KaimanovichVershik
